<!-- ============================== SUPPORT ============================== -->
<div class="view" data-view="support" hidden>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="pagehead">
        <h1 style="font-size:clamp(46px,7vw,100px)"><span class="chrome">You don’t have to figure this out alone.</span></h1>
        <p>You can call, text, chat, or read first. There is no perfect way to begin. These are U.S.-based starting points.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="crisis">
        <div class="panel"><b class="red">988</b><p><strong style="color:var(--silverw)">Call or text 988</strong> to talk with a crisis counselor, for you or someone you care about. Chat at <a href="https://chat.988lifeline.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">chat.988lifeline.org ↗</a></p></div>
        <div class="panel"><b class="red">911</b><p><strong style="color:var(--silverw)">Immediate danger.</strong> For an urgent threat to life or safety, a serious medical emergency, fire, or a crime in progress.</p></div>
        <div class="panel"><b class="chrome" style="font-size:40px">800-422-4453</b><p><strong style="color:var(--silverw)">Childhelp</strong>, 24/7, for questions or support about child abuse. Call or text.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:20px">GhostHeart is not a crisis, medical, legal, housing, or emergency service. These connect to outside organizations with their own services and privacy rules.</p>

      <!-- Full resource list, carried over from the current site's Resources page (same organizations, words and links) -->
      <div class="res-dir" id="resources">
        <p class="mono" style="margin:26px 0 4px">Start where you are</p>
        <h2 class="giant res-h">What feels closest today?</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--silver);margin:4px 0 12px">You do not need a diagnosis or the perfect words. Pick one place to start, or show every option.</p>
        <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Filter resources"><button type="button" class="chip on" data-filter="start" aria-pressed="true">Start here</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="crisis" aria-pressed="false">Crisis support</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="mental" aria-pressed="false">Mental health</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="safety" aria-pressed="false">Safety &amp; abuse</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="youth" aria-pressed="false">Youth &amp; family</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="lgbtq" aria-pressed="false">LGBTQ+ &amp; trans</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="housing" aria-pressed="false">Housing &amp; legal</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="veterans" aria-pressed="false">Veterans</button><button type="button" class="chip" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="false">Show everything</button></div>
        <div class="res-grid">
<article class="resource" data-tags="crisis" id="r01"><p class="card-kicker">Immediate</p><h3>911 Emergency Services</h3><p>For an urgent threat to life or safety, a serious medical emergency, fire, or a crime in progress.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Crisis</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="tel:911">Call 911</a><a class="button" href="https://www.911.gov/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">911.gov</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="crisis mental" id="r02"><p class="card-kicker">Crisis support</p><h3>988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</h3><p>Emotional support for you or someone you care about by call, text, or chat.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Crisis</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:988">Call 988</a><a class="button" href="sms:988">Text 988</a><a class="button" href="https://chat.988lifeline.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Chat</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="safety youth" id="r03"><p class="card-kicker">Child safety</p><h3>Childhelp National Child Abuse Hotline</h3><p>Questions or support about child abuse. A counselor can listen and help explain possible next steps, 24/7.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Youth</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:18004224453">Call 800-422-4453</a><a class="button" href="sms:18004224453">Text 800-422-4453 (send GO)</a><a class="button" href="https://childhelphotline.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Childhelp</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="start safety" id="r04"><p class="card-kicker">Relationship safety</p><h3>National Domestic Violence Hotline</h3><p>Support for relationship abuse, safety planning, and finding local services.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Safety</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:18007997233">Call 800-799-SAFE</a><a class="button" href="sms:88788">Text START to 88788</a><a class="button" href="https://www.thehotline.org/get-help/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Chat &amp; options</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="safety" id="r05"><p class="card-kicker">Sexual violence</p><h3>RAINN National Sexual Assault Hotline</h3><p>Support after sexual assault or abuse—for survivors and people who care about them, 24/7.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Safety</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:18006564673">Call 800-656-HOPE</a><a class="button" href="sms:64673">Text HOPE to 64673</a><a class="button" href="https://rainn.org/help-and-healing/hotline/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Chat &amp; options</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="start mental" id="r06"><p class="card-kicker">Treatment</p><h3>SAMHSA Find Help</h3><p>Find treatment and support for mental health, drug, or alcohol concerns. No diagnosis is required to start looking.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Mental health</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://www.samhsa.gov/find-help" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open SAMHSA Find Help</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="start mental" id="r07"><p class="card-kicker">Information</p><h3>NAMI HelpLine</h3><p>Information, practical guidance, and peer-informed support for mental health questions. This is not a crisis line.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Mental health</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="tel:18009506264">Call 800-950-NAMI</a><a class="button" href="sms:62640">Text NAMI to 62640</a><a class="button" href="https://www.nami.org/nami-helpline/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Hours &amp; options</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="safety youth" id="r08"><p class="card-kicker">Bullying</p><h3>StopBullying.gov</h3><p>Clear steps for young people, parents, and educators responding to bullying or cyberbullying.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Youth</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://www.stopbullying.gov/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open official guidance</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="start housing" id="r09"><p class="card-kicker">Local essentials</p><h3>211</h3><p>Find local help with food, housing, bills, transportation, health care, and other basic needs.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Basic needs</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:211">Call 211</a><a class="button" href="https://www.211.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Find your local 211</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="housing" id="r10"><p class="card-kicker">Housing</p><h3>HUD Housing Counseling</h3><p>Connect with a HUD-approved counselor about renting, homeownership, foreclosure, or homelessness.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Housing</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://www.hud.gov/counseling" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Find HUD counseling</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="housing" id="r11"><p class="card-kicker">Legal</p><h3>Legal Services Corporation</h3><p>Find nonprofit civil legal-aid organizations serving low-income people with civil legal problems.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Legal aid</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://www.lsc.gov/about-lsc/what-legal-aid/i-need-legal-help" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Find civil legal aid</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="safety youth" id="r12"><p class="card-kicker">Child welfare</p><h3>Child Welfare Information Gateway</h3><p>Federal information about child abuse reporting, prevention, foster care, adoption, and family support. This is not a crisis line.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Families</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://www.childwelfare.gov/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open the official gateway</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="crisis lgbtq" id="r13"><p class="card-kicker">LGBTQ+ youth</p><h3>The Trevor Project</h3><p>Free, confidential, 24/7 crisis support for LGBTQ+ young people by call, text, or chat.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">LGBTQ+</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:18664887386">Call 866-488-7386</a><a class="button" href="sms:678678">Text START to 678-678</a><a class="button" href="https://www.thetrevorproject.org/get-help/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Chat &amp; options</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="mental lgbtq" id="r14"><p class="card-kicker">Trans peer support</p><h3>Trans Lifeline</h3><p>Peer support from trans people for trans and questioning people, even when you are not in crisis. Check current hours.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Trans</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:18775658860">Call 877-565-8860</a><a class="button" href="https://translifeline.org/hotline/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Hours &amp; privacy</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="crisis veterans" id="r15"><p class="card-kicker">Veterans crisis</p><h3>Veterans Crisis Line</h3><p>24/7 crisis support for Veterans, service members, and people who care about them. VA enrollment is not required.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Veterans</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:988">Call 988, then press 1</a><a class="button" href="sms:838255">Text 838255</a><a class="button" href="https://www.veteranscrisisline.net/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Chat &amp; options</a></div></article>
<article class="resource" data-tags="housing veterans" id="r16"><p class="card-kicker">Veterans housing</p><h3>National Call Center for Homeless Veterans</h3><p>Housing help for Veterans who are homeless or may lose their housing, and for people supporting them, 24/7.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Veterans</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button crisis-primary" href="tel:18774243838">Call 877-424-3838</a><a class="button" href="https://department.va.gov/homeless/nationalcallcenter/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">VA housing help</a></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="res-privacy">
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="mono" style="margin:0 0 4px">Your privacy · Your choice</p>
          <h3>What “confidential” means at 988</h3>
          <p>You can receive support without giving your name or location. Confidential does not mean anonymous: 988 may receive your phone number or chat IP address, calls may be monitored or recorded for quality assurance, and information can be shared in limited circumstances such as imminent risk or when required by law.</p>
          <a href="https://988lifeline.org/confidentiality/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read 988’s privacy policy ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="mono" style="margin:0 0 4px">Need to leave this page quickly?</p>
          <p>Internet, call, and text activity can sometimes be monitored and may not be completely erasable. Use a safer device if you can. Clear history only if doing so will not raise suspicion.</p>
          <div class="row"><a class="btn red" href="https://www.weather.gov/">Leave this page</a><a class="btn ghost" href="https://www.thehotline.org/resources/how-to-clear-search-history-and-other-tech-safety-tips/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Technology-safety guidance ↗</a></div>
          <p class="note">Opens Weather.gov in this tab. It does not erase browser, call, or text history.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</main>

